<h2>What actually determines the price you're quoted</h2>
<p>Cardamom is one of the more genuinely volatile spice commodities we handle, and it moves through India largely via the Kerala/Idukki auction system — meaning prices can shift week to week even within a single harvest season, not just year to year. Five things drive the number on your specific quote: size grade (Bold 8mm+ commands a substantial premium over AGEB, AGS and smaller commercial grades — this alone can be the single biggest swing factor), colour grade (deep green over duller/yellowed pods), that season's crop size in the Idukki growing belt (monsoon timing and volume directly affect yield, and cardamom's limited growing geography means a weak season tightens supply sharply), auction-price trends at the time of your order, and currency plus Gulf-freight-rate movements. We don't quote a flat per-kilogram figure without your size and colour specification, because the auction market itself doesn't move on a flat basis.</p>
<p>Quotes are issued FOB, CIF or CFR against your specific size grade, colour grade, packaging and destination port. To get an accurate quote fast, tell us: target size grade (Bold/AGEB/AGS or your own spec), colour requirement, packaging format, quantity, and destination port.</p>
